# Build context for ouroboros-rest/Dockerfile.
#
# Named for the Dockerfile rather than the directory because that image builds from the
# **repository root** (it is a Yarn workspace and the lockfile lives there). BuildKit
# reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore ahead of <context>/.dockerignore, so this file governs
# that build and no other — a root .dockerignore would silently apply to every image in
# the repo, and an ouroboros-rest/.dockerignore would apply to nothing at all.
#
# It is an allow-list, as ouroboros-ui/Dockerfile.dockerignore is and for the same
# reason. With the whole repository as the context, a deny-list quietly grows a hole
# every time a directory is added at the root, and what leaks is not only size: docs/,
# .git/ and four sibling modules have no business in this image. Starting from `*` means
# a new path is excluded until someone says otherwise.

# Nothing, unless named below.
*

# The workspace root: what Yarn resolves, installs and pins from.
!package.json
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc.yml

# The sibling manifests. Yarn resolves every workspace before installing any of them, so
# an absent manifest is a failed --immutable install, not a smaller context. They are
# the manifests only — no sibling module's source enters this image.
!ouroboros-db/package.json
!ouroboros-engine/package.json
!ouroboros-ui/package.json

# This module.
!ouroboros-rest

# ...minus what is generated rather than written. None of it is portable between a laptop
# and the image: node_modules is resolved for the host platform, dist is the output of a
# previous build and the runtime stage takes its copy from the build stage instead, and
# .turbo and coverage are a task runner's and a test run's bookkeeping.
ouroboros-rest/node_modules
ouroboros-rest/dist
ouroboros-rest/coverage
ouroboros-rest/.turbo
ouroboros-rest/*.tsbuildinfo

# ...and minus prose and the container definition itself, none of which any stage reads.
# Excluding them is not about size — it is that editing a sentence in the README should
# not invalidate the build cache and rebuild the service. The `*.spec.ts` suites are
# deliberately *not* here: they cost nothing in the image, because tsconfig.build.json is
# what decides that, and a second list of exclusions here would be a second place for the
# same decision to be made differently.
ouroboros-rest/README.md
ouroboros-rest/Dockerfile
ouroboros-rest/Dockerfile.dockerignore

# ...and minus anything holding a real value. Nothing in the build reads an env file —
# every OURO_* variable is supplied to the container at run time — so the only way one
# could reach a layer is by accident. `**/` because the exclusion has to hold for every
# directory the lines above let in, not just the root.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
